on/math-academy-id "q-3778" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{x+16}=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have an indeterminate form of type $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty },$ so applying  L'Hopital's rule yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{x+16} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{[{x}^{2}-1]^{′}}{[x+16]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{2x}{1} \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-3778/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aeebf57f-21dc-558a-bec5-4e97a5b26de4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-3778"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-31585/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "45f7f7ff-fa85-556d-ac9b-fb6cf116a017" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31585/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "29f955b3-1f9d-5ebc-9826-4d116af6cf84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31585/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "96b91ed0-23a5-5a64-b958-be50242ffb32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31585/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "19d23dce-89ec-5bf3-8b43-cb25fdebb900" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31585/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer/id #uuid "02299284-7905-5e23-a99b-fab257fad339" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31585/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3289c5e-cad9-5a38-9f0d-b79099f92a16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-31585/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-31585/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-31585/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-31585/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-31585/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-31585/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-31585" :question/id #uuid "b1e8835d-2849-5c15-b2b3-5060e0821698" :question/math-academy-id "q-31585" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}-x-1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1}=$" :question/worked-solution "If we plug in $x=0$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}-x-1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[{e}^{x}-x-1]^{′}}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}-1}{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}-x-1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1} & =-{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[{e}^{x}-1]^{′}}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]^{′}} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{0}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-31585/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a41d750-ffd9-5226-9bd7-b763575870c1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-31585"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72335/selection/7bc54ef2cebd9c4cf6fef3072c83d13d0dfd6652d02cb9919fbcbc5497b7a408" :answer/id #uuid "cad86e4c-2b0f-506d-8803-4288769136a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72335/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer/id #uuid "bd470956-f46a-524f-93f6-7cfea4f61dc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72335/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "32d005f8-8c9d-5b1c-a2d5-30ae5e4fe9cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72335/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "653ab907-40cd-5543-b0cd-e07538abe574" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72335/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "8f0555b1-3de4-5f74-b04d-e9711990e5ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72335/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "76b9f4c3-b07d-5a7b-a386-ed4be8f82892" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72335/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer-field/choices ["q-72335/selection/7bc54ef2cebd9c4cf6fef3072c83d13d0dfd6652d02cb9919fbcbc5497b7a408" "q-72335/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" "q-72335/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-72335/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-72335/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72335" :question/id #uuid "5460231d-5ab3-5dda-afe5-f1c42598ed15" :question/math-academy-id "q-72335" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{2/{x}^{2}}}{(\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})}=$" :question/worked-solution "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are ${lim}_{x\\to 0}{e}^{2/{x}^{2}}=\\infty $ and ${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{2/{x}^{2}}}{(\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{[{e}^{2/{x}^{2}}]}^{′}}{{[\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{2/{x}^{2}}(-\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}})}{(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{4{e}^{2/{x}^{2}}\\cancel{(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}}{\\cancel{(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}} \\\\  & =4{lim}_{x\\to 0}{e}^{2/{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-72335/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f29435f-b112-5999-b0ca-9003d9e622e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72335"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115530/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer/id #uuid "b29bb4de-e2e0-56ba-9282-b1fdfe9636df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115530/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "90c1c08b-70e3-5e52-9c96-014e226f89a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115530/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "33ffd934-5f64-58c1-bfa8-cf43ec6a7b06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115530/selection/7bc54ef2cebd9c4cf6fef3072c83d13d0dfd6652d02cb9919fbcbc5497b7a408" :answer/id #uuid "0768e085-457d-5566-8f90-19a74d61576f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115530/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "f2e3162a-4e7a-5564-9884-12464ab6d7b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115530/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e5faff8-f4dc-5206-83e4-4a1fbb981af5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115530/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer-field/choices ["q-115530/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" "q-115530/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-115530/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" "q-115530/selection/7bc54ef2cebd9c4cf6fef3072c83d13d0dfd6652d02cb9919fbcbc5497b7a408" "q-115530/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115530" :question/id #uuid "1c16c119-1378-5409-b295-b09c8e50af75" :question/math-academy-id "q-115530" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\sqrt{x}=\\infty $ and ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{ln}^{2}⁡x=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[\\sqrt{x}]^{′}}{{[{ln}^{2}⁡x]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}})}{(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{x}{4\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[\\sqrt{x}]^{′}}{[4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}})}{(\\frac{4}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{x}{8\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\sqrt{x} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115530/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aeebf57f-21dc-558a-bec5-4e97a5b26de4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115530"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336935/field-1/0aae0f62f78e37f51f0f104e1616f1edea4079865fd21fc152944066b39dedfe" :answer/id #uuid "b5df862c-e599-5956-bcd4-c6e6ea300a52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336935/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6692dc66-2864-55c0-918e-b77305481098" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336935/field-1/0aae0f62f78e37f51f0f104e1616f1edea4079865fd21fc152944066b39dedfe" :answer-field/choices ["q-336935/field-1/0aae0f62f78e37f51f0f104e1616f1edea4079865fd21fc152944066b39dedfe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336935" :question/id #uuid "f06dd217-55b8-5f77-84e6-dcab94f6c615" :question/math-academy-id "q-336935" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\,{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{ln\\,(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we plug in $x=0$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{ln\\,(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{[ln\\,(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)]}^{′}}{[1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))}{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)}{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{ln\\,(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)} & =-\\frac{2}{3}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)}{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)]}^{′}}{{[(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)]}^{′}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336935/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a41d750-ffd9-5226-9bd7-b763575870c1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336935"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
